  "vulnerability_information": "## Summary:\nAn authenticated user can enumerate other users' directory entries, including ID, display name, and email address, even when the instance is configured to restrict user enumeration to same-group or exact-match scenarios.\n\nThe attacker-controlled entry point is the partial search term sent to [`ContactIntegrationController::autoComplete()`](https://github.com/nextcloud/mail/blob/v5.7.4/lib/Controller/ContactIntegrationController.php#L87) on the email composition page. That handler forwards the term into [`ContactsIntegration::getContactsWithName()`](https://github.com/nextcloud/mail/blob/v5.7.4/lib/Service/ContactsIntegration.php#L272), which calls [`doSearch()`](https://github.com/nextcloud/mail/blob/v5.7.4/lib/Service/ContactsIntegration.php#L235). `doSearch()` only checks `core.shareapi_allow_share_dialog_user_enumeration`; it does not apply the stricter share-enumeration controls that the product uses elsewhere, such as `shareapi_restrict_user_enumeration_to_group` and the related full-match restrictions.\n\n## Steps To Reproduce (including PoC):\n\nI used \"github.com/juliusknorr/nextcloud-docker-dev\" as test environment.\n\n- Nextcloud version: Nextcloud Hub 26 Winter (34.0.0 dev)\n- Nextcloud Mail version: 5.7.4\n\n1. Login as admin and add Mail app.\n\n{F5573031}\n\n2. Create two groups (e.g., g1, g2) and assign one user to each group (e.g., Alice to g1 and Bob to g2).\n\n{F5573036}\n\n3. Set \"Restrict account name autocompletion and system address book access to users within the same groups\" as **checked** at `Administration Settings > Sharing > Privacy settings for sharing`. This should make it so that Alice can’t find Bob.\n\n{F5573054}\n\n4. Logout and login as Alice. Go to the Mail tab and link any email service. Click `New message`.\n\n{F5573061}\n\n5. Open Devtools offered by browser (I used Firefox). Type `@b` or something like `@{keyword}` in `Write message ...` textarea block. **The members of unauthorized group will be enumerated in the Response from HTTP `GET http://nextcloud.local/index.php/apps/mail/api/contactIntegration/autoComplete/{keyword}`query.**\n\n{F5573074}\n\n## Impact\n\nAn authenticated user can bypass an administrator-configured user-enumeration restriction and enumerate users outside their allowed group scope, disclosing other groups' user identifiers, display names, and email addresses.",
